[ti:Somewhere in Blue]
[ar:Luna Park]
[al:Blue Reverie]
[00:00]The harbour folds its paper map
[00:04.50]A blue light catches on my sleeve
[00:09.125]The boats write little letters to the shore
[00:15]I tuck a quiet morning in my pocket
[00:23]And walk until the windows turn to sky
[00:31]Your footsteps take the slower street
[00:40]Mine stop to count the silver on the tide
[00:55]Somewhere in blue, a bell is ringing
[01:12]The day has room for one more sound
[01:31]We leave our names beneath the bridge
[01:55]The water carries every folded corner of the map beyond the lights
[02:24]And brings the morning round again
